<title>ITALY: Italy may mediate U.S. Helms-Burton row with EU.</title>
<headline>Italy may mediate U.S. Helms-Burton row with EU.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy said on Monday there was a possibility it may mediate between the United States and the European Union in a dispute over Washington's Helms-Burton law, which penalises foreign firms that do business with Cuba.</p>
<p>The foreign trade ministry said in a statement that a possible Italian mediation to end the trade controversy had been discussed by Minister Augusto Fantozzi and U.S. undersecretary of state Stuart Eizenstat.</p>
<p>The ministry, responding to an Italian media report, said the proposal was made by the Americans.</p>
<p>The Helms-Burton law, which has been condemned by all major U.S. trading partners, including Canada and Mexico, allows U.S. citizens to sue foreign firms that invest in property confiscated after Cuba's communist revolution in 1959.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom - 396 6782501</p>
</text>
